I assume the new response contract for this endpoint will be. Is it correct?

{noformat}{
   first_name: string | null;
   last_name: string | null;
   email: string | null;
   business_company_id: number | null;
}{noformat}

We can remove all the “nulls” if we want, but we will have to populate it with either default values or thrown errors, once we can have all use-cases on the DB today.

[~accountid:5f4ce513323607003808eeaa] 

{quote}If I understand correct, with our shadow groups we would still have to go to BP to get it. Was is the idea to get rid of the call to BP entirely?{quote}

Yes, let’s resolve it internally (within this Reseller’s API) with some true/false logic so that is not LIVE yet.

{quote}I can also see that although the endpoint is not used today it is returning the {{business_user_id}}, but we should not do it anymore, right?{quote}

This endpoint is already used in business-billing. Instead of returning {{business_user_id}} we will start returning:

{noformat}user_id: business_user_id | reseller_account_id
user_type: BUSINESS_USER | RESELLER{noformat}

Regarding nulls, if we we go with nulls, we will have to handle them all on business-billing side, currently {{first_name}} {{last_name}} and {{phone}} can not be null for a business-user. I think we should continue the same contract.

{code:sql}USE taxify_chat;
DROP PROCEDURE IF EXISTS update_in_loop;

DELIMITER $$
CREATE PROCEDURE update_in_loop()
BEGIN

DECLARE v_min_id, v_max_id BIGINT;
DECLARE v_batch_size INT DEFAULT 200;

DECLARE v_sleep_cnt INT DEFAULT 0;
DECLARE v_sleep_after INT DEFAULT 2000;
DECLARE v_sleep_time INT DEFAULT 5;


SELECT MIN(id), MAX(id) INTO v_min_id, v_max_id FROM `taxify_chat`.`chat_participant`;
SELECT v_min_id, v_max_id, v_batch_size;

WHILE v_min_id <= v_max_id DO

  UPDATE taxify_chat.chat_participant cp 
  JOIN chat c on c.id = cp.chat_id 
  SET cp.chat_status = c.status 
  WHERE 
    cp.id >= v_min_id 
    AND cp.id < v_min_id + v_batch_size
   AND c.status != 'created';

  SET v_min_id = v_min_id + v_batch_size;

  SET v_sleep_cnt = v_sleep_cnt + 1;
  SELECT v_min_id, v_sleep_cnt, v_sleep_after, v_min_id*100/v_max_id as done;

#    IF v_sleep_cnt > v_sleep_after THEN
#      SELECT CONCAT('Sleeping ', v_sleep_time, ' sec');
#      SELECT SLEEP(v_sleep_time);
#      SET v_sleep_cnt = 0;
#    END IF;

END WHILE;
END;
$$
DELIMITER ;

CALL update_in_loop();

DROP PROCEDURE IF EXISTS update_in_loop();{code}

