Hey, [~accountid:61e7c9bb85a2d6007051a7d6]! 

Apologies for the delay with this task. 

I have now checked all fraud reasons with the Fraud team and our KB is up to date. About the example you shared: I see the user was not blocked, but they were just suspended from reserving the scooter (or e-bike). The fraud action was _PASS,_ and we have instructions for it in the KB (l[ink to the article|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/6444342751250]): 

* {color:#006644}_If the user is located in Belgium, Denmark, Italy, the Netherlands, or Switzerland, advise them to_ {color}[{color:#006644}+_top up their Bolt Balance_+{color}|https://beehive.bolt.eu/customer_support/kb/articles/internal/4411171286034#h_01FNR002226K5KC63CES767DVV]{color:#006644} _with at least 2 euros (or the sum equal to 2 EUR in local currency) to rent a scooter or e-bike._{color}
* {color:#006644}_If the user is located in another country, inform the user about_ {color}[{color:#006644}+_pre-authorisation_+{color}|https://support.taxify.eu/hc/en-us/articles/7108948722962]{color:#006644} _and advise them to have sufficient funds in their bank account._{color}

{color:#006644}*_Additional information about pre-authorisation_*{color}{color:#006644}_: The amount of pre-authorisation is shown on the Calculation log page. If the user has a negative Bolt Balance, this sum can be added to the pre-authorisation sum. You may inform the user about the pre-authorisation amount if their Bolt Balance is negative._{color}

In such a case, there is no need to verify the user. 

Maybe your question got already solved, but if not, please check the KB article I linked and let us know if you have any questions about it, or if you come across a situation that is not described there. 

At the moment, I see no KB updates are necessary.

Eliise

