11-03 17:13 Sent to Sanitex to amend invoices. Discovered a couple of problematic areas:

# 2 stores were missing from Edisoft invoices. These stores took the longest to price check and validate. Edisoft invoices allowed me to spend 20-30 mins per invoice, while normal pdf invoices- 1-2 hours per invoice. Shared ILN codes with Sanitex to add them to automatic invoice sending;
# Issue with WMS rounding up F&V kg values. Not a single product that is purchased in kg was correct. My trust is on Sanitex side on this one, as they weigh before loading and register the correct weight. This is due to be fixed (need to follow up on Friday);
# Short-term will try to split Sanitex orders to have 2 invoices: 1 for F&V and the other for Groceries. This way we will minimise the discrepancies risk, as 80% of price discrepancies arise from F&V. Removing them from the general invoice will make it easier to price check, as commonly their invoices consist of 100-200 SKU lines (waiting for Sanitex response, follow up on Friday);
# Why some non-F&V products have different prices? Need to involve Cat team to enforce this.

